Z||000025||mrfixit58||04-25-2001||05:23 PM||||Cosmo - Ask Gary this question at the next Suncoast Fiero Club meeting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> . Remember, his car was stolen and spent three days at the bottom of a pond. After dragging it home and gutting the interior, draining all the fluids and hosing everything off, he let it dry out, reinstalled the gauges, computer, distributor, new fluids and fired that baby up. It seems to be no worse for the bath!<P>Cameron - The picture you posted looks more like someone using and old Fiero as erosion control (note the boulders, missing rear suspension). When I was stationed in north Dakota, I say may farmer's ponds lined with old cars and boulders to keep their field soil from filling their irrigation pond. There is no telling how much all those cars would be worth now.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
